.TH LOCAL-OPTIMIZE 1 "November 2026" "local-optimize 1.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
local-optimize \- run the local-first MCP/RAG engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B local-optimize
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B local-optimize
runs application entry points from /usr/lib/local-optimize using the shared
Python virtual environment and system model store provisioned under
/var/lib/local-optimize.
It does not create secrets, databases or agent configuration.
.PP
The Python interpreter is read from
.B LOCAL_OPTIMIZE_VENV ,
$APP_ROOT/venv, or /var/lib/local-optimize/venv.
.B LOCAL_OPTIMIZE_ROOT
can override the application directory for packaging checks.
.B LOCAL_OPTIMIZE_MODELS_DIR
can override the HuggingFace models directory.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B sync
Provision /var/lib/local-optimize/venv and synchronize HuggingFace and Ollama models.
.TP
.B models
Inspect or synchronize models (
.B status
|
.B sync
).
.TP
.B migrate
Apply PostgreSQL migrations. This does not migrate agents.
.TP
.B server
Run the FastAPI server.
.TP
.B watchdog
Run filesystem indexing.
.TP
.B mcp
Run the full local-only MCP server.
.TP
.B lmstudio-mcp
Run the read-only LM Studio MCP wrapper.
.TP
.B index
Index the registered project.
.TP
.B version
Print the package version.
.TP
.B help
Print command help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/local-optimize
Application files and lock/policy metadata.
.TP
.I ~/.config/local-optimize/secrets.env
User-managed secrets; never installed by the package.
.TP
.I /var/lib/local-optimize/venv
Provisioned shared Python 3.14 Intel XPU environment.
.TP
.I /var/lib/local-optimize/models
Provisioned shared HuggingFace models.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR python3 (1)
.PP
Full documentation is installed in /usr/share/doc/local-optimize/.
